From e583ab6cc23152dd9e9be9bfdd035a5abc178bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Senior Matthew <SeniorMatt@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 02:25:00 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 24/31] kcm_tablet: Device page with Display, Pen and Pad as
 sub-pages instead of a tab bar; tablet events created after the first frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Page type: Device (docs/page-design.md). C++ models, the stored tablet settings, calibration, ActionDialog and the three tab
contents (DisplayTab, StylusTab, PadTab, MissingPadTab) are unchanged and reused as they are. Not built yet.

Moved / renamed:
- main.qml: device combo only with 2+ tablets (single tablet: its name as a label) (kcm_tablet/tabletsModel); then three
  rows, each opening a sub-page with kcm.push: Display -> DisplayPage.qml, Pen -> PenPage.qml, Pad -> PadPage.qml
  (kcm_tablet/TabDisplay, TabPen, TabPad; these replace the NavigationTabBar, the tabs are unlike things). Display and Pen rows
  are hidden when only a pad exists (as before); Pad shows "No pad inputs found" when there is no pad (NoPadInputs).
  "Test Tablet…" stays a page action, kept visible; the user-space-driver warning and the empty state are unchanged
  (TestTablet, UserSpaceDriverNotice, NoTablet).
- New files: PageRow.qml (row content), DisplayPage.qml, PenPage.qml, PadPage.qml (thin SimpleKCM wrappers). Each sub-page pops
  itself when a tablet is removed or gains a pen/pad, and forwards settingsRestored to its content (DisplayPage also redraws the
  mapping, as main.qml used to).
- Markers added on controls in ActionDialog, Calibration, ExternalScreenMapping, PadTab, StylusTab, Tester and MissingPadTab whose
  inventory rows are text-only (labels unchanged) so --strict can prove them: now 0 lost for kcm_tablet; full check LOST 0.
- Removed from main.qml: cancelCalibration() and its Connections; they read properties that main.qml never had
  (calibrationWindowOpen, currentCalibrationSysName, calibrationWindow) so they could not run.
HIG ids: HIG-001/005/006 (order by use), HIG-057 (no tab bar of unlike things; sub-pages), HIG list rows with title and subtitle.

Speed cause: (1) all three tabs were behind one Loader but the Display tab was built on every device change and the tab bar,
the libwacom-backed pen/pad editors and TabletEvents (Wayland tablet protocol bind) came up with the page; now the main page is a
combo and three rows, StylusTab (548 lines, Shapes, pressure Canvas) and PadTab are only created when opened, and TabletEvents sits
in a Loader that is active only once a tablet exists. (2) libwacom database is still loaded at KCM creation (kcmtablet.cpp) and
is not moved here. After numbers: pending, manager will measure.

Unconfirmed: sub-page initial properties with a null InputDevice (properties are not "required" on the new pages for that reason);
the shell showing the page header title for pushed pages; Layout.fillHeight of DisplayTab/StylusTab directly under a ColumnLayout in
a SimpleKCM (was inside a Loader in the same kind of layout). Not compiled.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X5N5x9eWzmrq6QYrYLwQnk
